# Allowlisted CVEs. Every entry is dated and carries a reason, because the
# allowlist is the evidence of judgement: a gate with no allowlist either never
# fired or was quietly lowered, and neither is a defensible answer.
#
# The rule applied here: an entry is allowed only when Debian 13 has no fixed
# version AND the vulnerable code has no reachable caller in this image. Where a
# fix existed it was taken instead. `apt-get upgrade` in the Dockerfile cleared
# 20 HIGH findings in the util-linux family (CVE-2026-53612 through 53615) that
# would otherwise be sitting in this file, and taking a fix is always preferred
# to recording a reason not to.
#
# `ignore-unfixed` is deliberately NOT set on the scanner. Hiding every unfixed
# finding would erase exactly the judgement this file records.
#
# Reviewed 2026-08-22 against python:3.12-slim (Debian 13, trixie), and again
# 2026-09-07 after seven new advisories turned the gate red on `main`.
# Re-check when the base image is next bumped: an entry that outlives its
# reason is worse than no entry, because it reads as a decision somebody made.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# perl-base, 8 findings including 4 CRITICAL. 2026-08-22.
#
# perl arrives with the Debian base and this service never executes it. Nothing
# in the image shells out: the entry point is uvicorn, the request path is
# FastAPI into scikit-learn, and the health check is a python one-liner. It
# cannot be purged either, because dpkg depends on it.
#
# The real fix is a base without perl, which means distroless or a
# from-scratch image, and that is the open item recorded in the README rather
# than something to pretend away here.
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-9538

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# openssl, libssl3t64, openssl-provider-legacy. 2026-08-22.
# Debian marks this fix_deferred, so there is nothing to upgrade to.
# This container does not terminate TLS and makes no outbound TLS connection.
# It speaks plain HTTP on the container network; the Cloudflare Tunnel and the
# reverse proxy in front of it are what hold certificates. Revisit the moment
# this service is given a certificate or an outbound client.
CVE-2026-14456

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ncurses: libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin. 2026-08-22.
# A terminal library in a container that is never given a TTY and runs no
# terminal program. No fixed version in Debian 13.
CVE-2025-69720

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gzip. 2026-08-22.
# The gzip *binary* is never invoked. The dataset is gzipped and is read by
# Python's gzip module through zlib, at build time, from a file pinned by
# sha256 in this repository. There is no path from a request to this package.
CVE-2026-41992

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# libacl1. 2026-08-22.
# POSIX ACL library. The service sets no ACLs and writes nothing outside the
# container's own layer. No fixed version in Debian 13.
CVE-2026-54369

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# util-linux: bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1, libsmartcols1,
# libuuid1, login, mount, util-linux. 2026-09-07.
#
# Four advisories published after the 2026-08-22 review, all in mount and
# namespace handling: a failed external mount helper still running privileged
# X-mount post-hooks (76642), `nsenter --join-cgroup` leaking root (78408),
# X-mount.subdir detached-tree handling (78409), and restricted bind mounts not
# pinning their target (78410).
#
# Installed 2.41.5-0+deb13u1, which is already what `apt-get upgrade` in the
# Dockerfile pulls, and Debian 13 publishes no fixed version for any of the
# four. There is nothing to take.
#
# Every one of them needs a privileged mount, nsenter or bind-mount call, and
# this image can make none. Nothing in the runtime tree shells out: `tools/`
# is copied in the builder stage only and never reaches the runtime image, and
# `anomaly/` makes no subprocess call at all. The deployment then removes the
# capability these need: `capabilities.drop: [ALL]`, `privileged: false`,
# `allowPrivilegeEscalation: false`, `readOnlyRootFilesystem: true`, running as
# uid 10001 under the RuntimeDefault seccomp profile.
#
# Revisit if the pod is ever granted a capability back, given a writable
# volume, or if any runtime code starts a subprocess.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# sqlite: libsqlite3-0. 2026-09-07.
#
# Arbitrary code execution through crafted FTS5 input (11822) and arbitrary
# code execution or crash by the same route (11824). Installed
# 3.46.1-7+deb13u1, no fixed version in Debian 13.
#
# The library arrives with the Python base image and nothing here uses it.
# There is no database in this service: the request path is FastAPI into
# scikit-learn over a fitted estimator, and neither `anomaly/` nor any pinned
# dependency imports `sqlite3`. Reaching FTS5 at all requires the application
# to create and query a full-text table, which nothing in this repository does.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# systemd: libsystemd0, libudev1. 2026-09-07.
#
# Local privilege escalation in systemd-homed. Installed 257.13-1~deb13u1, no
# fixed version in Debian 13.
#
# The scan names libsystemd0 and libudev1, the shared libraries the base image
# carries as transitive dependencies. The vulnerable component is the
# systemd-homed daemon, and no init system runs in this container: PID 1 is
# uvicorn, per the Dockerfile CMD. There are also no user accounts here to
# escalate between, since the process runs as a single unprivileged uid.
CVE-2026-16742
